@@ -3,3 +3,25 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## Layout and conventions
+
+- `src/index.ts` is the public entry point. Tests live in `test/*.test.ts` and run with `npm test`
+  (`node --test`, Node ≥ 22.18 strips TypeScript types natively; no build step or dependency needed).
+  Keep to erasable TypeScript syntax (no `enum`, no parameter properties) so that keeps working.
+- Each feature follows its RFC strictly; the tests include the RFC's own examples.
+
+## Features
+
+### JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+- `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value the pointer refers to. It throws
+  `InvalidPointerError` for a malformed pointer (not empty and not starting with `/`, or a `~` not
+  followed by `0`/`1`) and `UnresolvablePointerError` when the pointer does not reach a value
+  (missing member, index out of bounds, `-`, index with leading zero or non-digits, stepping into a
+  scalar). Both extend `Error`.
+- Only own members of objects are looked up, so `/__proto__` or `/toString` never reach the prototype.
+- Building blocks for later features (e.g. JSON Patch): `parsePointer(pointer)` → unescaped tokens
+  (`""` → `[]`; decodes `~1` before `~0`), `formatPointer(tokens)` → pointer string, and
+  `parseArrayIndex(token)` → the index, or `undefined` if the token is not an RFC 6901 array index
+  (`-` is reported as `undefined`; callers that accept "append" must check for it themselves).
